.TH GENERATE_PDF_MAP 1 "September 2026" "Dragon GL" "Dragon GL DM Tools"
.SH NAME
generate_pdf_map \- render an ASCII floor dump as a color PDF map
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B generate_pdf_map.py
.I ascii_dump
.I output_pdf
.RI [ floor_number ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B generate_pdf_map.py
converts an ASCII floor dump produced by the Dragon GL server into a
readable, color-coded PDF map.

The script is used by the DM commands
.B dm_pdf
and
.B dm_mapfloor
after the server dumps the whole floor as an ASCII grid.

Each recognized map character is rendered using a dedicated color and is
also described in a legend. Unexcavated rock, represented by a space
character, is rendered using a dark background color.

The PDF contains a title identifying the floor and the dimensions of the
ASCII grid, followed by the rendered map and its legend.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I ascii_dump
Path to the ASCII floor dump to read.
The file is read as UTF-8 text and all rows are padded to the same width.
.TP
.I output_pdf
Path of the PDF file to create.
.TP
.I floor_number
Optional floor number to display in the PDF title.
If omitted, the script attempts to extract the floor number from the dump
filename using a pattern such as
.BR floor_7
or
.BR floor-7 .
If no floor number can be inferred, the label
.B Unknown
is used.
.SH MAP LEGEND
The following characters are recognized:
.TP
.B #
Wall / Obsidian
.TP
.B +
Door
.TP
.B ~
Water
.TP
.B L
Lava
.TP
.B >
Stairs Down
.TP
.B <
Stairs Up
.TP
.B $
Gold Vein
.TP
.B B
Crystal (Blue)
.TP
.B P
Crystal (Purple)
.TP
.B M
Glowing Mushroom
.TP
.B ,
Grass
.TP
.B .
Other / carved
.PP
A space character represents unexcavated rock and is rendered using the
map background color.
Any character not explicitly recognized is rendered using the same color
as
.B .
.SH DEPENDENCIES
The script requires Python 3 and the following Python packages:
.TP
.B reportlab
Required to create the PDF.
.TP
.B Pillow
Optional. When available, Pillow is used to render the map as a PNG before
embedding it in the PDF. If Pillow is unavailable, the script falls back
to drawing individual tiles directly with ReportLab.
.PP
On Fedora Linux, the required Python packages can be installed with:
.PP
.nf
python3 -m pip install --user reportlab pillow
.fi
.PP
Alternatively, install distribution packages when available:
.PP
.nf
sudo dnf install python3-reportlab python3-pillow
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. The PDF was written successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred. The error description is written to standard error.
.SH ERRORS
The script exits with status 1 when:
.IP \(bu 2
the command-line arguments are invalid;
.IP \(bu 2
the input dump cannot be read;
.IP \(bu 2
the input dump is empty;
.IP \(bu 2
a required Python dependency is missing; or
.IP \(bu 2
the PDF cannot be generated or written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a PDF and infer the floor number from the dump filename:
.PP
.nf
./generate_pdf_map.py map_dump_floor_7.txt floor_7.pdf
.fi
.PP
Explicitly specify the floor number:
.PP
.nf
./generate_pdf_map.py map_dump_floor_7.txt floor_7.pdf 7
.fi
.PP
The generated PDF title includes the floor number and the dimensions of
the ASCII grid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I map_dump_floor_*.txt
Typical ASCII floor dump files. The script does not require a particular
filename, but uses the filename to infer the floor number when the third
argument is omitted.
.SH NOTES
The character-to-color mapping is intended to remain synchronized with
the mapping used by
.B dm_pdf
and
.B dm_mapfloor
in
.BR src/server/server_commands.c .
.PP
The generated PDF uses a single page whose dimensions are calculated from
the dimensions of the input grid.
